The libraries.txt is a file which lists the Component Libraries which shall be used, apart from
the ones which are placed in the libraries folder*.
To add a file to this, simply open libraries.txt with a text editor and
add the path to that file in there. Please use one line for each path.

For example this would work well in MS Windows :
C:/ExternalLibrariesFolder/first_library.alib
C:/ExternalLibrariesFolders/another_library.alib

But this would not work:
C:/ExternalLibrariesFolder/first_library.alib C:/ExternalLibrariesFolders/another_library.alib

The easiest way to add a library is nevertheless to simply add the .alib-file into the libraries folder.

_________________________________________________________________________
 * Files that are placed in the libraries folder and that have a usable file ending, are added to Component Libraries
 even if they are not listed in libraries.txt
 CirNavSys regards files with the ending ".alib" usable.
